+// Reason: find_proc_info needs to locate the eh_frame / .debug_frame
+// for the procedure containing IP. The local-mode libunwind uses
+// `dl_iterate_phdr` to walk loaded objects and binary-searches their
+// embedded `.eh_frame_hdr` tables; we transcribe that here for
+// remote mode by calling the exported helper
+// `_Ux86_64_dwarf_find_proc_info` which does exactly that. The
+// coordinator runs in a request thread (not the signal handler), so
+// `dl_iterate_phdr` is safe — and the PHDR cache override (patches
+// 1+2) keeps it lock-free.
+// Reference: thirdparty libunwind/src/x86_64/Gfind_proc_info-lsb.c
+//   (`_Ux86_64_dwarf_find_proc_info` is the same code the local
